threshold (2.0.1-1) trixie; urgency=high

  * Fix application startup crash on every installed package (DEB, RPM,
    Void, AppImage): the Carbon UI's bundle and UserScript shim path
    lookup omitted the "dist/" directory segment that every packaging
    format actually installs to, so the app exited immediately with
    "Carbon bundle not found" on first launch. 2.0.0 never actually ran
    once installed from a package; this was only caught by launching the
    installed .deb for real, which no CI job did.
  * Ship web/dist/shim.js (the WebKit document-start UserScript) as part
    of the web build; it was previously read from a source-tree-only
    path with no installed fallback.
  * Add a real light mode: the UI had no light-theme CSS at all (every
    color was hardcoded dark), and the Dark mode switch's "off" state
    silently followed the system color scheme instead of forcing light,
    so turning it off did nothing visible on a system that itself
    prefers dark. The switch is now a direct on/off: off always renders
    light, on always renders dark. Also fixes the switch's own knob not
    staying in sync when appearance changes arrive outside the initial
    load.
  * CI pipeline repair: fixed a chain of issues that had kept every
    workflow run red since the 2.0.0 release cycle (missing evidence
    directory, a duplicate dpkg --configure call, invalid workflow YAML,
    pre-existing flake8 violations, a missing sudo dependency, the Void
    Linux job's chroot sandboxing, a stale EC manifest checksum, two
    self-referential file races, RPM verification gaps, and a canonical
    filename check that ignored the Debian revision suffix).

 -- Soubarna <Soubarna@live.in>  Sun, 27 Sep 2026 19:28:02 +0000

threshold (2.0.0-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Unified packages (issue #86): one complete DEB, one distribution-neutral
    Unified RPM (replaces the paired main + msi-ec-dkms release), and one
    self-contained x86-64 AppImage
  * Shared EC lifecycle authority owns setup, update, repair, boot
    reconciliation, and removal; DEB/RPM hooks invoke it without
    reimplementing lifecycle behavior
  * MSI DMI preflight: non-MSI systems never build or load msi-ec; EC
    failures never fail package installation
